Gateway connection-test diagnostic boundary
===========================================

Saved and unsaved gateway tests return fixed result messages instead of
arbitrary AdapterResult.message values. Successful checks report connection
success. Recognized AUTH_FAILED, CONN_FAILED and TIMEOUT codes produce fixed,
actionable guidance; unknown or malformed codes produce a generic failure.
Raised adapter exceptions retain the existing fixed exception categories.

The service's exception log records a fixed warning with the vendor, without
raw exception text or traceback. Other adapter and infrastructure logs are
not changed by this boundary. The existing service behavior already excluded
AdapterResult.error; error-only results remain explicit compatibility controls.

The qualification uses actual HTTP routes, service, encrypted credentials and
PostgreSQL. Authenticated state and adapter results are synthetic. Saved tests
retain destination and trust policy, update online/detected metadata as before,
and disconnect their owned adapter. The exact service logger is observed by a
temporary test handler. Before/after real TLS keepalive and cancellation checks
are additional transport regression controls, not diagnostic-privacy proofs.

Device hostname, model, version and other legitimate metadata remain provider
data; this is not a universal secret scrubber. Arbitrary provider metadata, other
operation logs and current caller/session/grant revalidation require separate
review. Saved-test resource scope and stale results are covered by
GATEWAY-TEST-AUTHORITY. Constructor exceptions are covered by
GATEWAY-CONSTRUCTION-FAILURES; saved-settings propagation is covered by
GATEWAY-SAVED-TEST-POLICY.
No database history rewrite, hardware write, schema or dependency change occurs.
